      "content": "This \"Run-time error '1004'\" often occurs when `Select` and `SpecialCells` are used in combination, which can sometimes fail depending on the worksheet's state. Try modifying your code to target the range directly instead of selecting it first. Change `ws.Select` and `ws.Range(\"C1:C100\").SpecialCells(xlCellTypeBlanks).Value = 0` to `ws.Range(\"C1:C100\").SpecialCells(xlCellTypeBlanks).Value = 0` without the preceding `ws.Select`. This should resolve the object-defined error.",
      "source": "target",
